    "title": "WNV and EEE Cases Confirmed in Georgia Horses - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Horse & Rider ,\n15 hours ago The Georgia Department of Agriculture recently reported that one horse in Sumter County has tested positive for West Nile virus (WNV) and one horse in Effingham County has tested positive for Eastern equine encephalitis (EEE). This is the second confirmed WNV and fourth confirmed EEE case in Georgia in 2025. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 2",
